<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>Inverted Pendulum / Control Lab</title><style>
*{box-sizing:border-box}body{margin:0;font:15px/1.5 -apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',sans-serif;color:#193548;background:#eef3f6}main{max-width:1180px;margin:24px auto;padding:32px;background:white;border-radius:20px}h1{font-size:36px;line-height:1.15;font-weight:600;margin:10px 0}h2{font-size:21px;font-weight:500}.eyebrow{font-size:11px;color:#158982;letter-spacing:2px}.muted{color:#617786}.controls{display:flex;gap:16px;align-items:end;flex-wrap:wrap;background:#f3f7f9;padding:16px;border-radius:12px;margin:22px 0}label{display:grid;gap:5px;font-size:12px;color:#617786}select,button{font:inherit;font-size:14px;padding:10px 14px;border:1px solid #cfdee5;border-radius:8px;background:white;color:#193548;min-height:42px;cursor:pointer}button.primary{background:#193548;color:white}input{accent-color:#158982;width:100%}.time{flex:1;min-width:180px}.comparison{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:22px}.rig{background:#f8fafb;padding:15px;border-radius:10px;min-width:0}.rig h2{margin:0}.rig canvas{width:100%;height:245px;display:block}.tag{font-size:12px;min-height:36px}.plots{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,minmax(0,1fr));gap:16px;margin:26px 0}.plots canvas{width:100%;height:230px;display:block}figure{margin:0;min-width:0}figcaption{font-weight:500}.legend{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:20px;font-size:12px;margin-top:18px}.legend i{display:inline-block;width:20px;border-top:3px solid #168982;vertical-align:middle;margin-right:6px}.legend .open{border-color:#d46b42}.legend .grey{border-color:#667783;border-top-style:dashed}.result{padding:14px 0;border-top:1px solid #dce6eb;border-bottom:1px solid #dce6eb;font-size:14px}details{margin-top:24px;font-size:13px}summary{cursor:pointer;font-size:15px;font-weight:500}code{background:#f1f5f7;padding:2px 4px}footer{font-size:12px;color:#617786;margin-top:28px}a{color:#137e83}@media(max-width:850px){.plots{grid-template-columns:1fr}}@media(max-width:640px){main{margin:6px;padding:18px}.comparison{grid-template-columns:1fr}h1{font-size:28px}.controls label{flex:1}}
</style></head><body><main><div class="eyebrow">CONTROL LAB / CONTROLLER COMPARISON</div><h1>The inverted pendulum</h1><p class="muted">One physical system. Three feedback designs. Explore the trade-off between recovery and actuator effort. Playback uses saved nonlinear simulations.</p>
<a href="double.html" style="display:inline-block;margin:12px 0;font-weight:600">Next experiment: double inverted pendulum →</a><p><a href="triple.html">Explore the triple pendulum →</a></p><div class="controls"><label>Experiment<select id="task"><option value="balance">Recover an initial tilt</option><option value="position">Reach a position target</option><option value="push">Reject a horizontal push</option></select></label><label>Initial tilt (deg)<select id="tilt"><option disabled>0</option><option>2</option><option selected>5</option><option>10</option></select></label><label>Controller<select id="method"><option value="feedback">Pole placement</option><option value="gentle">LQR — gentle</option><option value="responsive">LQR — responsive</option></select></label><button id="play" class="primary">Play</button><button id="reset">Restart</button><label class="time">Time: <span id="time-label">0.00 s</span><input id="time" type="range" min="0" max="12" step=".02" value="0" aria-label="Playback time in seconds"></label></div>
<p id="experiment" class="muted"></p><div class="comparison"><section class="rig"><h2>Without feedback</h2><p id="open-status" class="tag"></p><canvas id="open" role="img" aria-label="Uncontrolled cart and pendulum animation"></canvas></section><section class="rig"><h2 id="controller-title">Pole placement</h2><p id="feedback-status" class="tag"></p><canvas id="feedback" role="img" aria-label="Controlled cart and pendulum animation"></canvas></section></div>
<p class="muted" style="font-size:12px">Schematic animation. Positive angle leans right from vertical. Numerical plots use physical units. A stopped run freezes at its last state.</p>
<div class="legend"><span><i class="open"></i>Without feedback</span><span><i></i>Pole placement</span><span><i style="border-color:#7960bc"></i>LQR — gentle</span><span><i style="border-color:#2979bd"></i>LQR — responsive</span><span><i class="grey"></i>Target / external push</span></div>
<div class="plots"><figure><figcaption>Pendulum angle</figcaption><canvas id="angle" role="img" aria-label="Angle in degrees versus time"></canvas></figure><figure><figcaption>Cart position</figcaption><canvas id="position" role="img" aria-label="Cart position in metres versus time"></canvas></figure><figure><figcaption>Controller force</figcaption><canvas id="force" role="img" aria-label="Controller force in newtons versus time"></canvas></figure></div>
<div style="overflow-x:auto"><table id="metrics" style="width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;text-align:left;font-size:13px;margin:20px 0"></table></div><p class="muted" style="font-size:12px">Full-run metrics over 12 s. Effort is ∫u²dt in N²·s, not energy in joules. Lower effort alone does not imply better control. The unforced baseline uses no actuator force and can fall.</p><div id="result" class="result" aria-live="polite"></div>
<details open><summary>How LQR makes a choice</summary><p>LQR chooses feedback to minimise J = ∫(eᵀQe + Ru²)dt for the linear model, where e is the four-state error. Q = diag(10, 1, 100, 1) uses the documented SI state units. Gentle uses R = 4; responsive uses R = 0.1. The latter makes force less expensive relative to state error.</p><p>These are illustrative tuning choices, not a universal ranking. All three designs are tested on the same nonlinear model and ±8 N actuator limit. LQR optimality applies to its unconstrained linear design problem, not automatically to this saturated nonlinear simulation.</p></details><details open><summary>What to notice</summary><p>The controller initially moves the cart toward the falling pendulum. It must balance the angle while also bringing the cart back to its target. The feedback law uses all four states: position, velocity, angle and angular velocity.</p><p id="gain"></p><p>The controller comes from a linearisation near the upright equilibrium. Playback evaluates it on the nonlinear point-mass model with a ±8 N actuator limit. Passing these scenarios does not prove global stability.</p></details>
<details><summary>Model and experiment limits</summary><p>Cart mass: 0.8 kg. Pendulum bob: 0.2 kg. Massless rod: 0.5 m. Gravity: 9.81 m/s². Cart viscous friction: 0.08 N·s/m. Ideal full-state measurements, no delay and no sensor noise. The applied push is external to the actuator limit.</p><p>RK4 integration: 0.005 s. Display samples: 0.02 s. A run stops when |angle| exceeds 60° or |cart position| exceeds 2 m. This is an experiment cutoff, not a collision or rail-contact model.</p><p>Settling requires position error ≤ 0.02 m, angle ≤ 1°, speed ≤ 0.03 m/s and angular speed ≤ 0.05 rad/s for the rest of the run, with at least 1 s remaining. For the push experiment, the reported settling time is measured from the start and must occur after the push ends.</p><p>Next stages: sensor noise and observers. Swing-up is not included in this first experiment.</p></details>
<footer>Python source and saved results accompany this offline page. <a href="../README.md">Project guide</a>. No patient data or hardware control.</footer></main>
<script id="data" type="application/json">__DATA__</script><script>
(()=>{const D=JSON.parse(document.getElementById('data').textContent),$=s=>document.querySelector(s);const colours={open:'#d46b42',feedback:'#168982',gentle:'#7960bc',responsive:'#2979bd'},names={open:'Without feedback',feedback:'Pole placement',gentle:'LQR — gentle',responsive:'LQR — responsive'};const run=key=>c.runs[key==='feedback'?$('#method').value:key];let c,t=0,playing=false,last=0,raf=0;
function sample(rows,time){if(time<=rows[0][0])return rows[0];if(time>=rows.at(-1)[0])return rows.at(-1);let i=Math.min(rows.length-2,Math.max(0,Math.floor(time/.02)));while(i>0&&rows[i][0]>time)i--;while(i<rows.length-2&&rows[i+1][0]<time)i++;const f=(time-rows[i][0])/(rows[i+1][0]-rows[i][0]);return rows[i].map((v,k)=>v+f*(rows[i+1][k]-v))}
function setup(id,h){const el=$(id),w=el.clientWidth,d=devicePixelRatio||1;if(el.width!==Math.round(w*d)||el.height!==h*d){el.width=Math.round(w*d);el.height=h*d}const ctx=el.getContext('2d');ctx.setTransform(d,0,0,d,0,0);ctx.clearRect(0,0,w,h);return[ctx,w,h]}
function rig(key){const [ctx,w]=setup('#'+key,245),r=sample(run(key).data,t),x=w/2+r[1]*(w-50)/4,y=175,theta=r[3],colour=colours[key==='open'?'open':$('#method').value];ctx.strokeStyle='#c3d1db';ctx.lineWidth=2;ctx.beginPath();ctx.moveTo(15,y+30);ctx.lineTo(w-15,y+30);ctx.stroke();ctx.setLineDash([4,4]);const target=w/2+c.target*(w-50)/4;ctx.beginPath();ctx.moveTo(target,155);ctx.lineTo(target,217);ctx.stroke();ctx.setLineDash([]);ctx.fillStyle=colour;ctx.fillRect(x-30,y-6,60,23);ctx.fillStyle='#193548';for(const dx of [-20,20]){ctx.beginPath();ctx.arc(x+dx,y+23,7,0,Math.PI*2);ctx.fill()}ctx.strokeStyle=colour;ctx.lineWidth=5;ctx.beginPath();ctx.moveTo(x,y);ctx.lineTo(x+105*Math.sin(theta),y-105*Math.cos(theta));ctx.stroke();ctx.fillStyle=colour;ctx.beginPath();ctx.arc(x+105*Math.sin(theta),y-105*Math.cos(theta),10,0,Math.PI*2);ctx.fill();ctx.font='13px -apple-system,sans-serif';ctx.fillStyle='#193548';ctx.textAlign='center';ctx.fillText(`x = ${r[1].toFixed(2)} m     angle = ${(theta*180/Math.PI).toFixed(1)}°`,w/2,238);const m=run(key).metrics;$('#'+key+'-status').textContent=t>=m.end_time_s&&m.status!=='completed'?`Stopped at ${m.end_time_s.toFixed(2)} s: ${m.status==='tilt_limit'?'60° tilt limit':'2 m track limit'}`:c.task==='push'&&t>=4&&t<4.2?'External push: 3 N':'Actuator force: '+r[5].toFixed(2)+' N'}
function chart(id,column,factor,label){const [ctx,w,h]=setup('#'+id,230),left=52,right=w-12,top=18,bottom=189;const vals=Object.values(c.runs).flatMap(run=>run.data.map(r=>r[column]*factor));vals.push(0);if(id==='position')vals.push(c.target);if(id==='force'&&c.task==='push')vals.push(3);let lo=Math.min(...vals),hi=Math.max(...vals),pad=Math.max((hi-lo)*.12,.1);lo-=pad;hi+=pad;const X=a=>left+a/12*(right-left),Y=a=>bottom-(a-lo)/(hi-lo)*(bottom-top);ctx.strokeStyle='#dce6eb';ctx.lineWidth=1;ctx.strokeRect(left,top,right-left,bottom-top);ctx.font='11px -apple-system,sans-serif';ctx.fillStyle='#617786';for(let i=0;i<=4;i++){const v=lo+(hi-lo)*i/4;ctx.textAlign='right';ctx.fillText(v.toFixed(1),left-5,Y(v)+4);ctx.textAlign='center';ctx.fillText(i*3,X(i*3),bottom+16)}ctx.fillText('Time (s)',(left+right)/2,224);ctx.save();ctx.translate(12,(top+bottom)/2);ctx.rotate(-Math.PI/2);ctx.fillText(label,0,0);ctx.restore();for(const key of ['open','feedback','gentle','responsive']){ctx.strokeStyle=colours[key];ctx.lineWidth=2;ctx.beginPath();c.runs[key].data.forEach((r,i)=>i?ctx.lineTo(X(r[0]),Y(r[column]*factor)):ctx.moveTo(X(r[0]),Y(r[column]*factor)));ctx.stroke()}ctx.strokeStyle='#667783';ctx.setLineDash([4,4]);ctx.beginPath();if(id==='force'){for(const [a,b]of[[0,0],[4,0],[4,3],[4.2,3],[4.2,0],[12,0]]){const y=c.task==='push'?b:0;ctx.lineTo(X(a),Y(y))}}else{ctx.moveTo(X(0),Y(id==='position'?c.target:0));ctx.lineTo(X(12),Y(id==='position'?c.target:0))}ctx.stroke();ctx.setLineDash([]);ctx.strokeStyle='#193548';ctx.lineWidth=1;ctx.beginPath();ctx.moveTo(X(t),top);ctx.lineTo(X(t),bottom);ctx.stroke()}
function draw(){if(!c)return;$('#time').value=t;$('#time-label').textContent=t.toFixed(2)+' s';rig('open');rig('feedback');chart('angle',3,180/Math.PI,'Angle (deg)');chart('position',1,1,'Position (m)');chart('force',5,1,'Force (N)')}
function pause(){playing=false;cancelAnimationFrame(raf);$('#play').textContent='Play'}
function choose(){pause();t=0;const push=$('#task').value==='push';$('#tilt').disabled=push;$('#tilt').options[0].disabled=!push;if(push)$('#tilt').value='0';else if($('#tilt').value==='0')$('#tilt').value='5';c=D.cases.find(x=>x.task===$('#task').value&&x.tilt===Number($('#tilt').value));$('#experiment').textContent={balance:'Target: keep the pendulum upright and return the cart to x = 0 m.',position:'Target: keep the pendulum upright while moving the cart to x = 0.5 m.',push:'Both runs start exactly upright. A 3 N push acts from 4.0 to 4.2 s; the controller should recover x = 0 m.'}[c.task];const method=$('#method').value,m=c.runs[method].metrics;$('#controller-title').textContent=names[method];
$('#metrics').innerHTML='<thead><tr><th>Controller</th><th>Settling (s)</th><th>Peak |u| (N)</th><th>Effort (N²·s)</th></tr></thead><tbody>'+['feedback','gentle','responsive'].map(key=>{const v=c.runs[key].metrics;return `<tr style="color:${colours[key]};background:${key===method?'#f1f5f7':'transparent'}"><td style="padding:10px 5px">${names[key]}</td><td>${v.settling_time_s===null?'Not settled':v.settling_time_s.toFixed(2)}</td><td>${v.peak_force_N.toFixed(2)}</td><td>${v.force_squared_integral_N2s.toFixed(2)}</td></tr>`}).join('')+'</tbody>';
const gain=method==='feedback'?D.gain:D.lqr[method].gain;$('#gain').textContent='Selected feedback: u = clip(−K(s − s_target), −8, 8) N. K = ['+gain.map(v=>v.toFixed(3)).join(', ')+']. '+(method==='feedback'?'Desired poles: '+D.poles.join(', ')+' s⁻¹.':'LQR weights: Q = diag('+D.lqr[method].Q.join(', ')+'), R = '+D.lqr[method].R+'.');$('#result').textContent=`${names[method]} full-run result: ${m.status==='completed'?'completed 12 s':m.status}. Settling time: ${m.settling_time_s===null?'not achieved':m.settling_time_s.toFixed(2)+' s'}. Peak actuator force: ${m.peak_force_N.toFixed(2)} N.`;draw()}
function tick(now){if(!playing)return;t=Math.min(12,t+Math.max(0,Math.min((now-last)/1000,.1)));last=now;draw();if(t>=12)pause();else raf=requestAnimationFrame(tick)}
$('#play').onclick=()=>{if(playing)pause();else{if(t>=12)t=0;playing=true;last=performance.now();$('#play').textContent='Pause';raf=requestAnimationFrame(tick)}};$('#reset').onclick=()=>{pause();t=0;draw()};$('#method').onchange=choose;$('#task').onchange=choose;$('#tilt').onchange=choose;$('#time').oninput=e=>{pause();t=Number(e.target.value);draw()};document.addEventListener('visibilitychange',()=>{if(document.hidden)pause()});matchMedia('(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)').addEventListener('change',pause);let timer;new ResizeObserver(()=>{clearTimeout(timer);timer=setTimeout(draw,80)}).observe(document.querySelector('main'));$('#gain').textContent='Feedback law: u = clip(−K(s − s_target), −8, 8) N. K = ['+D.gain.map(v=>v.toFixed(3)).join(', ')+']. Desired poles: '+D.poles.join(', ')+' s⁻¹.';choose()})();
</script></body></html>
